	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Installation en Oracle linux]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=27101#p27101"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonsoir,<br />j&#039;ai téléchargé :<br />postgresql-9.6.8-1-linux-x64-binaries.tar.gz<br />ensuite j&#039;ai voulu suivre :<br />comme dit dans DBA1<br />PostgreSQL Administration (DALIBO)</p><p>$ tar xvfj postgresql-X.Y.Z.tar.bz2<br />$ cd postgresql-X.Y.Z<br />$ ./configure<br />$ make<br />$ make install<br />Mais :<br />Après tar xvf<br />[root@rac3 postgres]# ls -l<br />total 151408<br />drwxrwxr-x 9&#160; 501&#160; 501&#160; &#160; &#160; 4096 Feb 27 08:57 pgsql<br />-rwxr-x--- 1 root root 155036431 Mar 12 22:22 postgresql-9.6.8-1-linux-x64-binaries.tar.gz<br />Donc<br /> cd pgsql<br />[root@rac3 pgsql]# ./configure<br />bash: ./configure: No such file or directory</p><p>[root@rac3 pgsql]# find . -name configure<br />[root@rac3 pgsql]# cd bin<br />[root@rac3 bin]# ./configure<br />bash: ./configure: No such file or directory</p><p>Comment dois-je donc installer postgres?<br />Merci pour votre aide.</p>]]></content>
